<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH GOVT STILL MEETING, ECON PACKAGE DELAYED.</title>
<headline>CZECH GOVT STILL MEETING, ECON PACKAGE DELAYED.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The three governing coalition parties were still meeting on Wednesday at 3:00 p.m. (1500 GMT), delaying the unveiling of the government's package of pro-growth economic measures.</p>
<p>A government spokesman did not say how long the meeting would last, nor did he disclose any information on the meeting.</p>
<p>The government is expected to announce a sweeping series of measures aimed at jump starting the sluggish Czech economy.</p>
<p>It is still expected that the measures will be announced on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-000</p>
</text>
